This is a complete guide to building a "Product Management" application. We will use **Node.js/Express** for the backend (REST API), **MongoDB** for the database, and **React** for the frontend.

**Note:** Since you asked to "add dummy data," I will use an in-memory array to simulate a database for simplicity (so you don't need to install MongoDB right now), but the code structure remains professional.

---

### Prerequisites
Make sure you have installed:
*   [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (LTS version recommended)

---

### Step 1: Set Up the Project Structure
Create a main folder and a subfolder for the backend.

```bash
mkdir my-crud-app
cd my-crud-app
mkdir backend
```

---

### Step 2: Build the Backend (Node + Express)

1.  **Initialize the backend:**
    ```bash
    cd backend
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors nodemon
    ```

2.  **Create the file structure:**
    Create a file named `index.js` inside the `backend` folder.

3.  **Write the code (`backend/index.js`):**
    This includes the API routes and the **Dummy Data** logic.

    ```javascript
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');

    const app = express();
    app.use(cors());
    app.use(express.json());

    // --- DUMMY DATA ---
    let products = [
        { id: 1, name: "Laptop", price: 1200 },
        { id: 2, name: "Mouse", price: 25 },
        { id: 3, name: "Keyboard", price: 80 }
    ];

    let nextId = 4;

    // --- API ROUTES ---

    // GET all products
    app.get('/api/products', (req, res) => {
        res.json(products);
    });

    // GET single product
    app.get('/api/products/:id', (req, res) => {
        const product = products.find(p => p.id === parseInt(req.params.id));
        if (!product) return res.status(404).json({ message: "Product not found" });
        res.json(product);
    });

    // CREATE a product (Add Dummy Data)
    app.post('/api/products', (req, res) => {
        const newProduct = {
            id: nextId++,
            name: req.body.name,
            price: req.body.price
        };
        products.push(newProduct);
        res.status(201).json(newProduct);
    });

    // UPDATE a product
    app.put('/api/products/:id', (req, res) => {
        const index = products.findIndex(p => p.id === parseInt(req.params.id));
        if (index === -1) return res.status(404).json({ message: "Product not found" });

        products[index] = { ...products[index], ...req.body };
        res.json(products[index]);
    });

    // DELETE a product
    app.delete('/api/products/:id', (req, res) => {
        products = products.filter(p => p.id !== parseInt(req.params.id));
        res.json({ message: "Deleted successfully" });
    });

    // Start Server
    const PORT = 5000;
    app.listen(PORT, () => {
        console.log(`Server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
    });
    ```

